<% layout('layout/boilerplate.ejs') %>

<main>
  <section class="section container">
    <a href="/" class="back-link">&larr; Back</a>

    <div class="feature-card">
      <div class="feature-card-header">
        <span class="feature-card-dot"></span>
        <span class="feature-card-dot"></span>
        <span class="feature-card-dot"></span>
        <span class="title">ui-kits — voult.dev</span>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-card-body">
        <div class="feature-full">
          <h1>Pre-built UI kits</h1>
          <p class="feature-full-intro">
            Styling an auth flow is one of the less fun parts of shipping a product. You end up with a half-finished login page that doesn't match your brand and breaks on mobile. Our UI kits eliminate that.
          </p>

          <h2>What's included</h2>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Login &amp; register components</strong> — email/password forms, OAuth buttons, forgot-password flows, all pre-styled and interactive.</li>
            <li><strong>Multi-framework support</strong> — components are available for React, Vue, Svelte, and plain HTML. Pick the one that matches your stack.</li>
            <li><strong>Themed by default</strong> — dark mode, light mode, or custom. Uses CSS variables so you can override colors with a few lines of config.</li>
            <li><strong>Accessible out of the box</strong> — keyboard navigation, ARIA labels, focus management, and screen-reader testing are built in.</li>
            <li><strong>Yours to fork and customize</strong> — every kit is MIT licensed. Adapt the markup, restyle with your brand, or use it as-is.</li>
          </ul>

          <p>
            The goal is to spend your design time on what makes your product unique, not on yet another login form.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</main>
